# The Random Forest is trained as a negative result (see docs/dataset.md): 59 MB
# for a model the router never loads, because it is less accurate than XGBoost
# and spends the request's own latency scoring candidates. It is reproducible
# with `python ml/train.py`, so it is not carried in the repository. The served
# XGBoost artifact (1.7 MB) and the ridge baseline (2 KB) are committed.
models/random_forest_*.joblib